</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Haase</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>BioMOBY successfully integrates distributed heterogeneous bioinformatics Web Services. The PlaNet exemplar case</article-title><source>Plant Physiology</source><year>2005</year><volume>138</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15888673</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1104/pp.104.059170</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Turinsky</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ah-Seng</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Stromer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Taschuk</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Sensen</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bioinformatics visualization and integration with open standards: the Bluejay genomic browser</article-title><source>In Silico Biology</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>198</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15972014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>States</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bioinformatics code must enforce citation</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2002</year><volume>417</volume><fpage>588</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12050633</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/417588b</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Extensible Markup Language</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.w3.org/xml"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="